efinitely it does not worth the ticket price (1000 rupies)...", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2014-05-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "15D9F667FF498AC3C603E8B5C3A123EE", "name": "Silvia D", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/bibetta", "username": "bibetta", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/01/a4/0f/2d/bibetta.jpg", "contribution_count": 156, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 187849, "location_name": "Milan", "location_name_detailed": "Milan, Italy"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/3a/b6/66/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/3a/b6/6a/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/3a/b6/79/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/3a/b6/89/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/3a/b6/9a/pashupatinath-temple.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2015-01-21", "published_at_date": "2015-01-21"}, {"review_id": 250173990, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r250173990-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Spiritual reality", "text": "The building itself is very impressive and you will feel its aura soon as you step in.\nShoes etc will have to be kept outside where there are facilities for storage for free.\nNo foreigners are allowed in the temple but can view the site from across the river. The priests do not pester you for pujas and secuity will only let you view the deity for a few seconds. The cremating of the bodies below was a sobering sight of life and the river seemed polluted. You are free to spend as much time as you like and can enjoy the sights of the temple. A must visit place for all Hindus.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2015-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "0A2F53E21B9F366D32FAF384F3B56940", "name": "Kumar Morjaria", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/KumarMorjaria", "username": "KumarMorjaria", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/13/50/b4/46/kumarmorjaria.jpg", "contribution_count": 199, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 187055, "location_name": "Milton Keynes", "location_name_detailed": "Milton Keynes, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2015-01-20", "published_at_date": "2015-01-20"}, {"review_id": 249878355, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r249878355-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "The real Nepalese deal", "text": "If you want to get the real Nepalese deal, then go to this cremation site and sit watching the cremations together with the locals and the monkeys that roam freely! It sounds grim but it is fascinating. Be prepared for a culture shock as the river that that runs through this site is heavily polluted and there are actual burning pyres. \n\nLots of photo ops with 'swamis' dressed up to the nines for that very reason - to make a quick buck. Be generous, they make such an effort!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2014-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "9361BF87B6C0F97173732A4F92E428AF", "name": "otolith", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/otolith", "username": "otolith", "avatar": "http